\description{
Build, compare and interpret transcriptomic prediction models.

Build and compare transcriptomic prediction models for binary and right-censored survival outcomes. A common interface combines model specification, feature selection, shared-fold comparison, nested tuning, final fitting and independent-cohort evaluation. Saved predictions support discrimination, calibration, decision-curve analysis, feature stability, cohort-level synthesis and graphical reports. Reusing identical fold-local forest selections accelerates comparisons across multiple learners. Models are provided through native R engines with task-specific configurations. Native multiclass forests, multinomial regularized regression, discriminant analysis, naive Bayes and classification trees support independent feature analysis and shared-fold model evaluation.
}
